# Amazon S3 Basics

## Date

May 29, 2026

## Goal

Learn the basics of Amazon S3, understand how buckets work, and practice managing files in cloud storage.

## AWS Services Used

- Amazon S3

## What I Did

- Logged into the AWS Management Console
- Opened the Amazon S3 service
- Explored the S3 interface and learned where buckets and objects are managed
- Uploaded image files to an S3 bucket
- Organized files into folders
- Moved files between folders
- Deleted files I no longer needed

## What I Learned

- Amazon S3 is AWS's object storage service.
- Buckets are containers used to store objects such as images, videos, and documents.
- Objects can be uploaded, organized, moved, and deleted through the S3 console.
- The S3 interface makes it easy to manage cloud storage resources.

## Problems I Ran Into

- I accidentally placed an image in the wrong folder within my S3 bucket.
- I had to figure out how object management works in Amazon S3 and how to move files between locations.
- By exploring the S3 console, I learned how to relocate objects and organize bucket contents correctly.
- This helped me better understand how S3 stores and manages objects.

